################################################################################
# 2d deposition rate calibration: ask for a speed, get that speed
#
# A flat front normal to x, driven by a rate given in length/time, so the
# answer is arithmetic rather than a simulation result: the surface is asked
# to advance at 1.0 length/time and f_ablate[21], the front speed the surface
# actually realized, must come back equal to it.  The residual few-percent
# excess is a documented artifact of the finite domain height (cells where
# the forced horizontal boundary front meets the vertical one are oblique and
# over-read; their weight falls as the domain gets taller).
#
# The corner point field is a linear ramp in x read with push no, so the
# isosurface is the plane where the ramp crosses thresh and its normal is
# exactly the x axis.  A binary 0/255 field could not carry that direction,
# and the front would not move at the requested speed; see the smooth
# keyword of read_isurf.
#
# There is no gas: this is a pure test of the corner point arithmetic.
#   f_ablate     = summed corner point values, the material present
#   f_ablate[21] = realized front speed, which must equal the requested 1.0
#   f_ablate[22] = corner point value change actually applied at the last
#                  event; the f_ablate scalar moves by exactly this amount
#
#  - The "comm/sort" option to the "global" command is used to match MPI runs.
################################################################################

seed                12345
dimension           2
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes

boundary            r r p

create_box          0 20 0 80 -0.5 0.5
create_grid         20 80 1
balance_grid        rcb cell

global              nrho 1.0 fnum 1.0

species             ../ablation/air.species N
mixture             air N

variable            rate grid 1.0
fix                 ablate ablate all 1 1.0 v_rate mode deposit &
                    units distance

global              surfs implicit
read_isurf          all 20 80 1 ramp.20x80 127.5 ablate push no

surf_collide        1 diffuse 300.0 1.0
surf_modify         all collide 1

timestep            0.001

stats               10
stats_style         step f_ablate f_ablate[21] f_ablate[22]

run                 50
